  {
    "id": "621f9a5f-1cb6-4ccf-a122-5a193a7f3c80",
    "code": "3X3-CFOP-F2L-01-FL",
    "case_set_id": "d983f542-c510-4272-81ce-8a7af2e1638a",
    "title": "F2L 1+",
    "long_name": "F2L 1 FL",
    "kind": "f2l",
    "pattern_from": "Cross",
    "pattern_to": "2 Layers",
    "scramble": "F' L F L'",
    "notes": null,
    "story": "<!-- Case: F2L-01-FL -->\n\n## Overview\nMirror of the foundational FR insert: a paired block floats above the Front Left slot and drops straight in with pure L-moves.\n\n## Recognition\n- White/D-color sticker sits on top of the corner directly above its matching edge.\n- From the front, both stickers that should face left already line up into a 2×1 block.\n- A single `U` or `U'` move centers the block over FL with perfect color alignment.\n\n## Technique\n1. Use `U`/`U'` to position the block over FL.\n2. Insert using `L' U L`, keeping the right hand free for look-ahead.\n3. If FL is occupied, eject with `L' U' L`, realign, and reinstate the pair.\n\n## Fingertricks\n- Anchor your left thumb on the front-left sticker so `L' U L` feels stable.\n- Use the right index for `U` to avoid regripping.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n- Forgetting to clear the FL slot before inserting.\n- Misaligning the block and forcing `L' U L`, which twists the pair.\n\n## Practice\n- Alternate 10 reps between this mirror and F2L-01-FR to balance both hands.\n- Time goal: achieve sub‑0.9s inserts while maintaining look-ahead.\n\n## Related Cases\n- [F2L-01-FR](deddal://case/F2L-01-FR) – Right-hand version.\n- [F2L-02-FL](deddal://case/F2L-02-FL) – Paired block parked over the opposite slot.\n\n## Pro Tips\n- Because your right hand stays idle, use it to track the next pair or start AUF planning early.",
