    "pattern_to": "2 Layers",
    "scramble": "L F' L' F",
    "notes": null,
    "story": "<!-- Case: F2L-02-FL -->\n\n## Overview\nPaired block belongs in the Front Left slot but floats over FR; open the front face, swing it across with L-moves, then close the door.\n\n## Recognition\n- Corner and edge stay paired yet sit above FR with stickers facing right.\n- FL slot is empty, letting you safely use `F`/`F'` without breaking other progress.\n- After `F'`, the block aligns perfectly with the left face—clear sign that `L F L'` will finish the job.\n\n## Technique\n1. Execute `F'` to bring the block into the front layer.\n2. Apply `L F L'` while the slot is exposed to insert the pair on the left.\n3. Restore the front face (`F`) to return to standard orientation.\n\n## Fingertricks\n- Push `F'` with your right index, then switch to left-hand control for `L F L'`.\n- Keep your right hand ready to start tracking the next pair while the front layer closes.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n- Rotating the cube instead of using the front-face transfer, which wastes time.\n- Forgetting to restore the front face, leaving the cross misaligned.\n\n## Practice\n- Drill 5 sets alternating between this case and the FR version to stay comfortable on both sides.\n- Focus on keeping the cube steady during `F'`/`F` so you can look ahead mid-insert.\n\n## Related Cases\n- [F2L-02-FR](deddal://case/F2L-02-FR) – Right-hand counterpart solved via rotation.\n- [F2L-03-FL](deddal://case/F2L-03-FL) – Another front-layer insert when the corner is already in the slot.\n\n## Pro Tips\n- Visualize the front layer as a “door” you temporarily open—this mental model keeps the move count low and helps in walkthrough explanations.",
