    "pattern_from": "Cross",
    "pattern_to": "2 Layers",
    "scramble": "F U' F'",
    "notes": null,
    "story": "<!-- Case: F2L-03-FL -->\n\n## Overview\nFront-left keyhole: the corner sits in the slot facing you, the matching edge rests on top, and a quick `F U F'` cycle pairs and inserts without touching the right side.\n\n## Recognition\n- Front face shows a vertical 1×2 bar of the left color (edge stacked over corner).\n- The corner’s white sticker looks at you, signalling it’s flipped in the slot.\n- The top edge sticker matches the front center, so opening the slot is safe.\n\n## Technique\n1. Use `F` to open the slot and bring the corner into the top layer.\n2. Perform `U`/`U'` to align the edge with its center so it joins the corner.\n3. Finish with `F'` to seal the slot and drop the paired block back into FL.\n\n## Fingertricks\n- Push `F`/`F'` with the right index while the left hand handles `U`.\n- Keep your left thumb anchored on the front face so the slot opens cleanly.\n\n## Common Mistakes\n- Closing the slot before the edge is aligned, which recreates the same flip.\n- Overshooting the front-layer turns and disturbing adjacent solved pieces.\n\n## Practice\n- Alternate between this mirror and F2L-03-FR to stay balanced.\n- Run 10 reps focusing on keeping the rest of the cube perfectly still during `F` moves.\n\n## Related Cases\n- [F2L-03-FR](deddal://case/F2L-03-FR) – Right-hand equivalent.\n- [F2L-10-FL](deddal://case/F2L-10-FL) – Another flipped-corner scenario solved by hide-and-insert.\n\n## Pro Tips\n- Because the right hand is idle, use it to start AUF planning or point out cues during walkthrough explanations.",
